<section class="wz-hero"><div class="wz-w wz-hero-g"><p class="wz-vert" aria-hidden="true">WEARZEN</p><div class="wz-hero-i"><svg class="wz-enso" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M100 18c46 0 82 36 82 82s-36 82-82 82-82-36-82-82c0-38 26-70 62-79" pathLength="1"/></svg><figure class="rv-w rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1589713680561-1d0b6945a582?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=960&q=75" alt="a woman in a simple neutral top resting her hand against her face" width="720" height="960" fetchpriority="high"></figure><span class="wz-seal" aria-hidden="true">WZ</span></div><div class="wz-hero-t"><p class="wz-ey">A calm wardrobe</p><h1>Wear less.<br>Wear <em>well</em>.</h1><p class="wz-lead">An independent guide to building a smaller, calmer wardrobe of natural fabrics and pieces you love to wear.</p><a class="wz-btn" href="capsule-wardrobe-guide.html">Begin with the capsule</a></div></div></section>

<section class="wz-ma"><div class="wz-w"><p class="wz-ma-q rv">The most beautiful wardrobe is the one where <em>everything</em> is worn.</p><svg class="wz-stroke" viewBox="0 0 600 30" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18C120 6 240 26 360 14S540 10 596 16" pathLength="1"/></svg></div></section>

<section class="wz-s wz-cp" id="capsule"><div class="wz-w wz-cp-g"><div><p class="wz-ey">Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">The capsule counter</h2><p class="wz-p">A few pieces that all work together make more outfits than you might think. Set your numbers and watch the combinations grow.</p>
<div class="wz-steps"><div class="wz-st"><span>Tops</span><button type="button" data-k="0" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer tops">&minus;</button><output id="cp-0">5</output><button type="button" data-k="0" data-d="1" aria-label="More tops">+</button></div><div class="wz-st"><span>Bottoms</span><button type="button" data-k="1" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer bottoms">&minus;</button><output id="cp-1">3</output><button type="button" data-k="1" data-d="1" aria-label="More bottoms">+</button></div><div class="wz-st"><span>Layers</span><button type="button" data-k="2" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer layers">&minus;</button><output id="cp-2">2</output><button type="button" data-k="2" data-d="1" aria-label="More layers">+</button></div><div class="wz-st"><span>Shoes</span><button type="button" data-k="3" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer shoes">&minus;</button><output id="cp-3">2</output><button type="button" data-k="3" data-d="1" aria-label="More shoes">+</button></div></div><figure class="wz-cp-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1693443688057-85f57b872a3c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=340&q=75" alt="a grey linen shirt on a hanger" width="620" height="340" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="wz-cp-o"><p class="wz-cp-n"><b id="cp-n">0</b><span>outfits from <i id="cp-p">0</i> pieces</span></p><div class="wz-grid" id="cp-g" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="wz-p" id="cp-t" aria-live="polite"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="wz-s wz-fb" id="fibre"><div class="wz-w"><div class="wz-fb-h"><p class="wz-ey">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">The fibre finder</h2><p class="wz-p">Choose the season and what matters most to you. We will rank the natural fibres that suit.</p></div>
<div class="wz-fb-g"><div class="wz-fb-c"><fieldset><legend>Season</legend><div class="wz-tabs" id="fb-s"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Warm</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Mild</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Cold</button></div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>What matters most</legend><div class="wz-tabs" id="fb-p"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Breathes</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Few creases</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Easy care</button><button type="button" data-v="3">Softness</button></div></fieldset><figure class="wz-fb-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1666112514265-a432cd607ce1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=340&q=75" alt="soft swirls of natural fabric" width="620" height="340" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<ol class="wz-bars" id="fb-o" aria-live="polite"></ol></div></div></section>

<section class="wz-s wz-gl"><div class="wz-w"><div class="wz-gl-h"><p class="wz-ey">Still life</p><h2 class="rv">Quietly worn</h2></div><div class="wz-gg"><figure class="wz-gi wz-gi0 rv"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1759229874810-26aa9a3dda92?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=900&q=75" alt="a woman in a black dress against a wooden wall" width="700" height="900" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Black, simply</figcaption></figure><figure class="wz-gi wz-gi1 rv"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1713881676551-b16f22ce4719?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=640&q=75" alt="a white linen shirt on a hanger" width="700" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Linen shirt</figcaption></figure><figure class="wz-gi wz-gi2 rv"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1707369707420-a1cde10f035a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=900&q=75" alt="a woman in a long neutral outfit on a beach" width="700" height="900" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Long lines</figcaption></figure><figure class="wz-gi wz-gi3 rv"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614631446501-abcf76949eca?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=640&q=75" alt="a calm, minimal open wardrobe" width="700" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>An edited rail</figcaption></figure><figure class="wz-gi wz-gi4 rv"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1625899845678-3fad6a4a1846?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=640&q=75" alt="neutral clothes and accessories laid out flat" width="700" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Laid out</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="wz-s wz-kn"><div class="wz-w wz-kn-g"><div class="wz-kn-h"><p class="wz-ey">Five principles</p><h2 class="rv">A wardrobe practice</h2><p class="wz-kn-n"><b data-count="33">33</b><span>pieces for three months is a popular capsule challenge</span></p></div><ol class="wz-kn-l"><li class="rv"><span>01</span><div><h3>One in, one out</h3><p>When something new arrives, something you no longer wear leaves.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>02</span><div><h3>Natural first</h3><p>Linen, cotton, wool and silk breathe, soften and age with grace.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>03</span><div><h3>A quiet palette</h3><p>Neutrals and one or two accent colours make everything work together.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>04</span><div><h3>Fit over fashion</h3><p>A well-fitting plain piece outlasts any trend.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>05</span><div><h3>Care is wear</h3><p>Washing gently and mending early doubles a garment's life.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="wz-gd"><div class="wz-w wz-gd-g"><a class="wz-gc rv" href="capsule-wardrobe-guide.html"><svg class="wz-enso" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M100 18c46 0 82 36 82 82s-36 82-82 82-82-36-82-82c0-38 26-70 62-79" pathLength="1"/></svg><span>Guide one</span><b>Building a Capsule Wardrobe</b><em>Edit, choose a palette, fill the gaps.</em></a><a class="wz-gc rv" href="natural-fabrics-guide.html"><svg class="wz-enso" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M100 18c46 0 82 36 82 82s-36 82-82 82-82-36-82-82c0-38 26-70 62-79" pathLength="1"/></svg><span>Guide two</span><b>A Guide to Natural Fabrics</b><em>Linen, cotton, wool, silk and hemp.</em></a></div></section>

